page":"https://rubyonrails.org","size":275235,"stargazers_count":57965,"watchers_count":57965,"language":"Ruby","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":22063,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1385,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["activejob","activerecord","framework","html","mvc","rails","ruby"],"visibility":"public","forks":22063,"open_issues":1385,"watchers":57965,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Since upgrading to Rails 3.2.12, we get behaviour along the lines of:\n\n```\n$ bundle exec rake db:drop && bundle exec rake db:create && bundle exec rake db:migrate\nrake aborted!\nCould not find table 'users'\n```\n\nIn our application, this means we can no longer migrate a DB from scratch.  However, I imagine that this issue could have further reaching implications.\n\nI created a basic app illustrating this issue: https://github.com/fraser/migration-error-3.2.12.  In particular, the commit https://github.com/fraser/migration-error-3.2.12/commit/a2836cf0b45e003cf01263844d60c8cf4a028670 shows the required changes for reproduction.\n\nI think what is happening is:\n\n```\n$ bundle exec rake db:migrate\n=> loads environment\n=> loads observers\n=> loads UserObserver\n=> loads User\n=> evaluates scope :id_0, where(:id => 0)\n=> executes engine.connection.schema_cache in ActiveRecord::PredicateBuilder\n=> schema doesn't exist since we haven't run migrations yet\n=> Could not find table 'users'\n```\n\nI am pretty sure this issue was introduced by https://github.com/rails/rails/commit/921a296a3390192a71abeec6d9a035cc6d1865c8#L3R54.\n\nThanks,\n\nFraser\n","reactions":{"url":"ht